{"title":"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> is a square and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f57cea90175beee710454564fe742c93d6411c85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PTQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> is an equilateral triangle.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>What is the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d785362c4ca299d0925aa981fe644abd152c30e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle TPR$\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/327c5a2374eda7cbb3d944fce161e89ad4e5f6fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 90^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 105^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 120^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 150^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 75^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"462\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d785362c4ca299d0925aa981fe644abd152c30e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle TPR$\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" /> is made up of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a139107de5cc38cefde6ed95eabfcc0a90fc7c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle TPQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab56c134c7ae517715af6c3beb90a1068a621a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle QPR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> in the diagram. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/b/28b1613a44f5705bd66494cc115b72d6f43fda11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle TPR = m \\angle TPQ + m \\angle QPR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"260\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> is a square and has a diagonal, the acute angles of the two right triangles in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> must measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d3f11ab7a3e93c7a404a34224228f0449505a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349d6d9248df6b07ce3f534750bfe29606cb7c8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PTQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is equilateral, all of its interior angles are equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We now know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6c3e1c4a5b2b3def9a6225bf0a09cf2d552f655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle TPQ = 60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b07d59a6ccb77ba430e0ab98f5a0e7a5c38ffdf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle QPR = 45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />. Plugging this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/b/28b1613a44f5705bd66494cc115b72d6f43fda11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle TPR = m \\angle TPQ + m \\angle QPR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"260\" height=\"18\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8afa6e215d7eaa2b5a9996862c3bbf9d7cb608f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle TPR = 60^{\\circ} + 45^{\\circ} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 105^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"275\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat\">2013 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\"